  "description": "Write intents x25519-xc20p-seal (spec §3.8), sealed to seal_pub[e] of seal-key.json seal_keys (vault shared). The target is the secret name (and optional purpose and sensitivity) an MCP client asked a human to write; it never carries a value. epk = X25519(ephemeral_secret, 9); shared = X25519(ephemeral_secret, seal_pub) (all-zero: bad_request); key = HKDF-SHA256(ikm=shared, salt=epk || seal_pub, info=utf8(\"akv1/write-intent\"), L=32); aad = cjson({\"ctx\":\"akv1/write-intent\",\"vault_id\",\"request_id\",\"key_epoch\",\"origin\",\"operation\",\"ts\",\"expires_at\"}); ct = XChaCha20-Poly1305(key, n, cjson(target), aad). cases: sealWriteIntent with the given ephemeral_secret, nonce wire.n and request_id MUST reproduce wire byte for byte, and openWriteIntent(SealSK[key_epoch], wire, {vault_id}) MUST yield target. openWriteIntent order: parse (v or alg unknown: unsupported_version; exact keys, IDs, epk 32 B, n 24 B, ct 16..16400 B, origin as in sealed-op.json, operation \"create\" or \"replace\", ts, expires_at > ts: bad_request); vault_id other than expected (bad_request); all-zero shared secret (bad_request); AEAD failure (decrypt_failed); pt not canonical, no name, unknown keys, purpose over 200 or an unknown sensitivity (bad_request). invalid: open the wire with SealSK of open_with_epoch and MUST fail with expect_error. seal_invalid: sealWriteIntent MUST refuse target with expect_error.",
